    "cpu.max": "400000 100000",
    "memory.max": "17179869184"
  },
  "changes": [
    "Capture intrinsic JSON parse/stringify before guest hooks; frame JSON as UTF-8 lines on real Unix duplex sockets.",
    "Own the transport in Open/Disconnecting/Closed phases; close descriptors on transition, queue callback/message/disconnect jobs on the canonical asynchronous dispatcher, and derive automatic child-process channel references from actual message/disconnect listeners.",
    "Match Node small/large UTF-8 write completion timing and libuv socket buffer capacities; native policy stays in Rust and ordinary functions/Control class are thin existing bridges.",
    "Fork clones options, forces shell false, defaults IPC and inherited/silent stdio, applies execPath/execArgv and removes inherited eval arguments with actual JavaScript strict equality.",
    "Reuse one CommonJS resolver for entry files/directories and require resolution.",
    "Unix fs-owned descriptors use their actual OS numbers; checked temporary duplicates allow inherited descriptor read/write/sync without transferring ownership. Non-Unix descriptor allocation remains unchanged.",
    "Rust determines whether Readable.pipe ends its destination; stdout/stderr stay open and source close shares the existing unpipe cleanup."
  ],
  "validation": {
